    "narrative": "The primary anchor for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, whose elite projection of 85.94 stands in a tier of its own. He benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Paredes, combining a potent lineup spot (Assumed #3) with a massive 25% boost from Park and SP skill, making him our primary source for stolen bases and counting stats. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang** also present strong profiles, both cracking the 68+ efficiency mark. **Brice Turang** is particularly intriguing; his 4% boost due to a slow opposing pitcher delivery creates a high-leverage scenario for stolen bases, a key scarcity target for our roster construction. **James Wood** remains a high-floor play at 65.62, bolstered by an elite 0.404 xwOBA that mitigates the slight park penalty he faces today.\n\nWe are navigating significant risk across the bottom of our lineup, with several spots relying on pending lineups. **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Kyle Karros** are all slotted in the #9 hole, which drags their efficiency scores down by 8%. While the matchup against Brandon Young provides a necessary SP-skill boost, these players are essentially banking on home-run potential or high-volume on-base opportunities to provide value. The most difficult bench decision was opting to sit **Max Muncy** (46.69); despite his potential, he was squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-ceiling players, and his reliance on a tough matchup against Detmers kept his efficiency just below the threshold required to displace the current starters.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding the heavy reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Kyle Karros**. Any deviation from the projected batting orders will necessitate a real-time re-evaluation of our daily game caps. Furthermore, while **Seiya Suzuki** and **Tyler Soderstrom** have the raw talent to perform, their efficiency scores are hampered by sub-optimal matchups against Cease and Detmers, respectively. These players are on a short leash, and we will monitor the game flow closely to ensure we aren't burning limited caps on sub-40 efficiency performances.",
